---
NIFT_TANSTACK_DOCUMENT_V1
{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You have a React Native or Expo app and you want to add streaming AI chat\nwithout putting provider SDKs or API keys in the native bundle. By the end of\nthis guide, your app will call a server-owned Hono route with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-react"},{"type":"text","value":", stream responses over a mobile-compatible transport, and\nkeep "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":" / "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENAI_MODEL"},{"type":"text","value":" on the server."}]},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Coming from the web quick start?"}]},{"type":"text","value":" The hook is the same, but the URL and\ntransport are different. React Native needs an absolute backend URL, not\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/api/chat"},{"type":"text","value":", and most Expo runtimes should start with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xhrHttpStream()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"1-install-packages","children":[{"type":"text","value":"1. Install packages"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you are starting from scratch, create an Expo app first:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"local-install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"create-expo-app@latest\",\"my-ai-chat\"]]},\"mode\":\"local-install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Install TanStack AI, the React hook package, the OpenAI adapter for your\nserver, and Hono for the example backend:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"@tanstack/ai\",\"@tanstack/ai-react\",\"@tanstack/ai-openai\",\"hono\",\"@hono/node-server\",\"zod\"]]},\"mode\":\"install\"}"}},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If your Expo app lives in a workspace, run the command from the app package or\nuse your workspace filter."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"2-keep-openai-on-the-server","children":[{"type":"text","value":"2. Keep OpenAI on the server"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create a Hono route that owns the model, API key, and response format. The\nnative app sends chat messages to this route; it never imports\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-openai"},{"type":"text","value":" and never receives "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// server.ts\nimport { serve } from '@hono/node-server'\nimport { chat, toHttpResponse, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { Hono } from 'hono'\nimport { model } from './config'\n\nconst app = new Hono()\n\nfunction requireOpenAIKey() {\n  if (!process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY) {\n    throw new Error('OPENAI_API_KEY is not configured on the server')\n  }\n}\n\napp.get('/health', (c) => c.json({ ok: true }))\n\napp.post('/chat/http', async (c) => {\n  requireOpenAIKey()\n  const body = await c.req.json()\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(model),\n    messages: body.messages,\n  })\n\n  return toHttpResponse(stream, {\n    headers: {\n      'Content-Type': 'application/x-ndjson',\n      'Cache-Control': 'no-cache',\n    },\n  })\n})\n\napp.post('/chat/sse', async (c) => {\n  requireOpenAIKey()\n  const body = await c.req.json()\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(model),\n    messages: body.messages,\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n})\n\nserve({\n  fetch: app.fetch,\n  hostname: '0.0.0.0',\n  port: Number(process.env.PORT ?? 8787),\n})","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set server-only environment variables where the Hono process runs:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...\nOPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.2","lang":"env"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run the Hono server before starting the native app. For a TypeScript-only\nexample, install "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tsx"},{"type":"text","value":" and add a script:"}]},{"type":"component","name":"tabs","attributes":{"variant":"package-manager","mode":"dev-install"},"children":[],"properties":{"data-package-manager-meta":"{\"packagesByFramework\":{\"react\":[[\"tsx\"]]},\"mode\":\"dev-install\"}"}},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm pkg set scripts.dev:server=\"tsx server.ts\"\npnpm dev:server","lang":"bash"},{"type":"blockquote","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"strong","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Route pairing matters:"}]},{"type":"text","value":" "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xhrHttpStream()"},{"type":"text","value":" and "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchHttpStream()"},{"type":"text","value":" expect\nthe newline-delimited JSON response from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toHttpResponse()"},{"type":"text","value":".\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xhrServerSentEvents()"},{"type":"text","value":" expects the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"text/event-stream"},{"type":"text","value":" response from\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toServerSentEventsResponse()"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"3-configure-a-native-reachable-url","children":[{"type":"text","value":"3. Configure a native-reachable URL"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"React Native is not served from your backend origin, so "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/api/chat"},{"type":"text","value":" cannot work\nas a default. Expose the backend URL to Expo with a public variable:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"EXPO_PUBLIC_TANSTACK_AI_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.10:8787","lang":"env"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the address your device can reach:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"iOS simulator: "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"http://127.0.0.1:8787"},{"type":"text","value":" often works."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Android emulator: use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"http://10.0.2.2:8787"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Physical device: use your computer's LAN IP, for example\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"http://192.168.1.10:8787"},{"type":"text","value":", or a tunneled HTTPS URL."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Only "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"EXPO_PUBLIC_*"},{"type":"text","value":" values are bundled into the app. Keep provider keys as\nplain server variables such as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"4-use-usechat-in-your-native-screen","children":[{"type":"text","value":"4. Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"useChat"},{"type":"text","value":" in your native screen"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Start with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xhrHttpStream()"},{"type":"text","value":" for Expo and React Native. It reads the same\nnewline-delimited JSON produced by "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toHttpResponse()"},{"type":"text","value":" and relies on XHR progress\nevents, which are usually more reliable on phone runtimes than streaming\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"code","value":"// ChatScreen.tsx\nimport { useState } from 'react'\nimport { Button, ScrollView, Text, TextInput, View } from 'react-native'\nimport { useChat, xhrHttpStream } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nconst baseUrl =\n  process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_TANSTACK_AI_BASE_URL ?? 'http://127.0.0.1:8787'\n\nexport function ChatScreen() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState('')\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, error } = useChat({\n    connection: xhrHttpStream(`${baseUrl}/chat/http`),\n  })\n\n  async function send() {\n    const text = input.trim()\n    if (!text || isLoading) return\n    setInput('')\n    await sendMessage(text)\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <View style={{ flex: 1, padding: 24, gap: 12 }}>\n      <ScrollView style={{ flex: 1 }}>\n        {messages.map((message) => (\n          <View key={message.id} style={{ marginBottom: 16 }}>\n            <Text style={{ fontWeight: '700' }}>{message.role}</Text>\n            {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\n              part.type === 'text' ? (\n                <Text key={index}>{part.content}</Text>\n              ) : null,\n            )}\n          </View>\n        ))}\n      </ScrollView>\n\n      {error ? <Text style={{ color: 'crimson' }}>{error.message}</Text> : null}\n\n      <TextInput\n        value={input}\n        onChangeText={setInput}\n        editable={!isLoading}\n        placeholder=\"Ask for a recipe...\"\n        style={{ borderWidth: 1, borderRadius: 8, padding: 12 }}\n      />\n      <Button title={isLoading ? 'Streaming...' : 'Send'} onPress={send} />\n    </View>\n  )\n}","lang":"tsx"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You now have a native chat screen that calls your server endpoint, streams\nassistant text, and keeps provider credentials outside the app."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"5-choose-a-transport-deliberately","children":[{"type":"text","value":"5. Choose a transport deliberately"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use the transport that matches your server route and runtime:"}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Native runtime"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Client adapter"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Server response"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Most Expo / React Native apps"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xhrHttpStream(url)"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/chat/http"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toHttpResponse(stream)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"SSE-compatible native runtime or proxy path"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xhrServerSentEvents(url)"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/chat/sse"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)"}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Runtime with streaming "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch"},{"type":"text","value":" support"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchHttpStream(url)"},{"type":"text","value":" with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/chat/http"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toHttpResponse(stream)"}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Only use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchHttpStream()"},{"type":"text","value":" when your exact runtime supports all of:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response.body"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response.body.getReader()"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TextDecoder"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If any of those are missing, the adapter throws\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UnsupportedResponseStreamError"},{"type":"text","value":". A polyfilled "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch"},{"type":"text","value":" that buffers the whole\nresponse is not enough; TanStack AI needs incremental response bytes to update\nthe chat while the model is streaming."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For deeper adapter options such as headers, credentials, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"withCredentials"},{"type":"text","value":", and\ndynamic URLs, see "},{"type":"link","href":"../transports/request-options","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Request Options"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"6-try-the-expo-recipe-example","children":[{"type":"text","value":"6. Try the Expo recipe example"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you are evaluating React Native support, use the included Expo app. It runs a\nlocal Hono/OpenAI server, shows a transport selector, and streams structured\nrecipe cards so you can verify native chat and structured output behavior\ntogether."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/ts-react-native-chat/.env"},{"type":"text","value":":"}]},{"type":"code","value":"OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...\nOPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.2","lang":"env"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Run the example:"}]},{"type":"code","value":"pnpm --filter ts-react-native-chat dev","lang":"bash"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The command starts:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Hono on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"0.0.0.0:8787"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expo/Metro in LAN mode"}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"EXPO_PUBLIC_TANSTACK_AI_BASE_URL=http://<lan-ip>:8787"},{"type":"text","value":" when a LAN address is detected"}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Scan the Expo Go QR code from a phone on the same Wi-Fi network. In the app,\nuse the Testing mode panel to switch between Fetch HTTP, XHR HTTP, and XHR SSE.\nThe main recipe card streams structured fields such as title, ingredients,\nsteps, tips, warnings, and revision across follow-up prompts."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"For example-specific commands and network overrides, see\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"examples/ts-react-native-chat/README.md"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"troubleshooting","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Troubleshooting"}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"http-localhost-8081-shows-json","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"http://localhost:8081"},{"type":"text","value":" shows JSON"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"That is normal. Port "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"8081"},{"type":"text","value":" is Metro's manifest and bundle server, not a web UI.\nLaunch the app from Expo Go, an Android emulator, or an iOS simulator instead."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"a-physical-device-cannot-reach-the-backend","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A physical device cannot reach the backend"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Open "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"http://<lan-ip>:8787/health"},{"type":"text","value":" from the phone browser. If it does not return\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{\"ok\":true}"},{"type":"text","value":", confirm the phone and computer are on the same Wi-Fi network,\nclient isolation is disabled, and your firewall allows Node.js on the Hono port\nand Metro port "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"8081"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"android-emulator-cannot-reach-127-0-0-1","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Android emulator cannot reach "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"127.0.0.1"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Use "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"http://10.0.2.2:8787"},{"type":"text","value":" for\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"EXPO_PUBLIC_TANSTACK_AI_BASE_URL"},{"type":"text","value":". Android emulators map "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"10.0.2.2"},{"type":"text","value":" to the\nhost machine."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"expo-prints-android-sdk-or-adb-warnings","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Expo prints Android SDK or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"adb"},{"type":"text","value":" warnings"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"This is an Android tooling issue, not a TanStack AI transport issue. Confirm\nAndroid Studio installed the SDK, an emulator exists in Device Manager, and\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"adb"},{"type":"text","value":" is on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"PATH"},{"type":"text","value":". On Windows, check\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Android\\Sdk\\platform-tools\\adb.exe"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"the-phone-logs-unsupportedresponsestreamerror","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The phone logs "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"UnsupportedResponseStreamError"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your runtime does not expose streaming "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Response.body.getReader()"},{"type":"text","value":", or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"TextDecoder"},{"type":"text","value":". Switch from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetchHttpStream()"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xhrHttpStream()"},{"type":"text","value":" or\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xhrServerSentEvents()"},{"type":"text","value":". Do not rely on fetch polyfills unless they provide a\nreal incremental readable stream."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":3,"id":"xhr-reports-a-server-error","children":[{"type":"text","value":"XHR reports a server error"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Check the Hono server terminal first. Common causes are missing\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENAI_API_KEY"},{"type":"text","value":", an unsupported "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"OPENAI_MODEL"},{"type":"text","value":", or pointing\n"},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"xhrServerSentEvents()"},{"type":"text","value":" at "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/chat/http"},{"type":"text","value":" instead of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"/chat/sse"},{"type":"text","value":" (or the reverse)."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"You now have the full React Native path: a server-owned provider boundary, a\nnative-reachable URL, a mobile-compatible transport, and an Expo example that\nproves the setup on a real device."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"1-install-packages","text":"1. Install packages","level":2},{"id":"2-keep-openai-on-the-server","text":"2. Keep OpenAI on the server","level":2},{"id":"3-configure-a-native-reachable-url","text":"3. Configure a native-reachable URL","level":2},{"id":"4-use-usechat-in-your-native-screen","text":"4. Use useChat in your native screen","level":2},{"id":"5-choose-a-transport-deliberately","text":"5. Choose a transport deliberately","level":2},{"id":"6-try-the-expo-recipe-example","text":"6. Try the Expo recipe example","level":2},{"id":"troubleshooting","text":"Troubleshooting","level":2},{"id":"http-localhost-8081-shows-json","text":"http://localhost:8081 shows JSON","level":3},{"id":"a-physical-device-cannot-reach-the-backend","text":"A physical device cannot reach the backend","level":3},{"id":"android-emulator-cannot-reach-127-0-0-1","text":"Android emulator cannot reach 127.0.0.1","level":3},{"id":"expo-prints-android-sdk-or-adb-warnings","text":"Expo prints Android SDK or adb warnings","level":3},{"id":"the-phone-logs-unsupportedresponsestreamerror","text":"The phone logs UnsupportedResponseStreamError","level":3},{"id":"xhr-reports-a-server-error","text":"XHR reports a server error","level":3}]},"frameworks":["react"],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYou have a React Native or Expo app and you want to add streaming AI chat\nwithout putting provider SDKs or API keys in the native bundle. By the end of\nthis guide, your app will call a server-owned Hono route with `useChat` from\n`@tanstack/ai-react`, stream responses over a mobile-compatible transport, and\nkeep `OPENAI_API_KEY` / `OPENAI_MODEL` on the server.\n\n> **Coming from the web quick start?** The hook is the same, but the URL and\n> transport are different. React Native needs an absolute backend URL, not\n> `/api/chat`, and most Expo runtimes should start with `xhrHttpStream()`.\n\n## 1. Install packages\n\nIf you are starting from scratch, create an Expo app first:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\nreact: create-expo-app@latest my-ai-chat\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nInstall TanStack AI, the React hook package, the OpenAI adapter for your\nserver, and Hono for the example backend:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-react @tanstack/ai-openai hono @hono/node-server zod\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nIf your Expo app lives in a workspace, run the command from the app package or\nuse your workspace filter.\n\n## 2. Keep OpenAI on the server\n\nCreate a Hono route that owns the model, API key, and response format. The\nnative app sends chat messages to this route; it never imports\n`@tanstack/ai-openai` and never receives `OPENAI_API_KEY`.\n\n```ts\n// server.ts\nimport { serve } from '@hono/node-server'\nimport { chat, toHttpResponse, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { Hono } from 'hono'\nimport { model } from './config'\n\nconst app = new Hono()\n\nfunction requireOpenAIKey() {\n  if (!process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY) {\n    throw new Error('OPENAI_API_KEY is not configured on the server')\n  }\n}\n\napp.get('/health', (c) => c.json({ ok: true }))\n\napp.post('/chat/http', async (c) => {\n  requireOpenAIKey()\n  const body = await c.req.json()\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(model),\n    messages: body.messages,\n  })\n\n  return toHttpResponse(stream, {\n    headers: {\n      'Content-Type': 'application/x-ndjson',\n      'Cache-Control': 'no-cache',\n    },\n  })\n})\n\napp.post('/chat/sse', async (c) => {\n  requireOpenAIKey()\n  const body = await c.req.json()\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(model),\n    messages: body.messages,\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n})\n\nserve({\n  fetch: app.fetch,\n  hostname: '0.0.0.0',\n  port: Number(process.env.PORT ?? 8787),\n})\n```\n\nSet server-only environment variables where the Hono process runs:\n\n```env\nOPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...\nOPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.2\n```\n\nRun the Hono server before starting the native app. For a TypeScript-only\nexample, install `tsx` and add a script:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"dev-install\" -->\n\nreact: tsx\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n```bash\npnpm pkg set scripts.dev:server=\"tsx server.ts\"\npnpm dev:server\n```\n\n> **Route pairing matters:** `xhrHttpStream()` and `fetchHttpStream()` expect\n> the newline-delimited JSON response from `toHttpResponse()`.\n> `xhrServerSentEvents()` expects the `text/event-stream` response from\n> `toServerSentEventsResponse()`.\n\n## 3. Configure a native-reachable URL\n\nReact Native is not served from your backend origin, so `/api/chat` cannot work\nas a default. Expose the backend URL to Expo with a public variable:\n\n```env\nEXPO_PUBLIC_TANSTACK_AI_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.10:8787\n```\n\nUse the address your device can reach:\n\n- iOS simulator: `http://127.0.0.1:8787` often works.\n- Android emulator: use `http://10.0.2.2:8787`.\n- Physical device: use your computer's LAN IP, for example\n  `http://192.168.1.10:8787`, or a tunneled HTTPS URL.\n\nOnly `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` values are bundled into the app. Keep provider keys as\nplain server variables such as `OPENAI_API_KEY`.\n\n## 4. Use `useChat` in your native screen\n\nStart with `xhrHttpStream()` for Expo and React Native. It reads the same\nnewline-delimited JSON produced by `toHttpResponse()` and relies on XHR progress\nevents, which are usually more reliable on phone runtimes than streaming\n`fetch`.\n\n```tsx\n// ChatScreen.tsx\nimport { useState } from 'react'\nimport { Button, ScrollView, Text, TextInput, View } from 'react-native'\nimport { useChat, xhrHttpStream } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nconst baseUrl =\n  process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_TANSTACK_AI_BASE_URL ?? 'http://127.0.0.1:8787'\n\nexport function ChatScreen() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState('')\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, error } = useChat({\n    connection: xhrHttpStream(`${baseUrl}/chat/http`),\n  })\n\n  async function send() {\n    const text = input.trim()\n    if (!text || isLoading) return\n    setInput('')\n    await sendMessage(text)\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <View style={{ flex: 1, padding: 24, gap: 12 }}>\n      <ScrollView style={{ flex: 1 }}>\n        {messages.map((message) => (\n          <View key={message.id} style={{ marginBottom: 16 }}>\n            <Text style={{ fontWeight: '700' }}>{message.role}</Text>\n            {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\n              part.type === 'text' ? (\n                <Text key={index}>{part.content}</Text>\n              ) : null,\n            )}\n          </View>\n        ))}\n      </ScrollView>\n\n      {error ? <Text style={{ color: 'crimson' }}>{error.message}</Text> : null}\n\n      <TextInput\n        value={input}\n        onChangeText={setInput}\n        editable={!isLoading}\n        placeholder=\"Ask for a recipe...\"\n        style={{ borderWidth: 1, borderRadius: 8, padding: 12 }}\n      />\n      <Button title={isLoading ? 'Streaming...' : 'Send'} onPress={send} />\n    </View>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nYou now have a native chat screen that calls your server endpoint, streams\nassistant text, and keeps provider credentials outside the app.\n\n## 5. Choose a transport deliberately\n\nUse the transport that matches your server route and runtime:\n\n| Native runtime | Client adapter | Server response |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Most Expo / React Native apps | `xhrHttpStream(url)` with `/chat/http` | `toHttpResponse(stream)` |\n| SSE-compatible native runtime or proxy path | `xhrServerSentEvents(url)` with `/chat/sse` | `toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)` |\n| Runtime with streaming `fetch` support | `fetchHttpStream(url)` with `/chat/http` | `toHttpResponse(stream)` |\n\nOnly use `fetchHttpStream()` when your exact runtime supports all of:\n\n- `Response.body`\n- `Response.body.getReader()`\n- `TextDecoder`\n\nIf any of those are missing, the adapter throws\n`UnsupportedResponseStreamError`. A polyfilled `fetch` that buffers the whole\nresponse is not enough; TanStack AI needs incremental response bytes to update\nthe chat while the model is streaming.\n\nFor deeper adapter options such as headers, credentials, `withCredentials`, and\ndynamic URLs, see [Request Options](../transports/request-options).\n\n## 6. Try the Expo recipe example\n\nIf you are evaluating React Native support, use the included Expo app. It runs a\nlocal Hono/OpenAI server, shows a transport selector, and streams structured\nrecipe cards so you can verify native chat and structured output behavior\ntogether.\n\nCreate `examples/ts-react-native-chat/.env`:\n\n```env\nOPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...\nOPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.2\n```\n\nRun the example:\n\n```bash\npnpm --filter ts-react-native-chat dev\n```\n\nThe command starts:\n\n- Hono on `0.0.0.0:8787`\n- Expo/Metro in LAN mode\n- `EXPO_PUBLIC_TANSTACK_AI_BASE_URL=http://<lan-ip>:8787` when a LAN address is detected\n\nScan the Expo Go QR code from a phone on the same Wi-Fi network. In the app,\nuse the Testing mode panel to switch between Fetch HTTP, XHR HTTP, and XHR SSE.\nThe main recipe card streams structured fields such as title, ingredients,\nsteps, tips, warnings, and revision across follow-up prompts.\n\nFor example-specific commands and network overrides, see\n`examples/ts-react-native-chat/README.md`.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### `http://localhost:8081` shows JSON\n\nThat is normal. Port `8081` is Metro's manifest and bundle server, not a web UI.\nLaunch the app from Expo Go, an Android emulator, or an iOS simulator instead.\n\n### A physical device cannot reach the backend\n\nOpen `http://<lan-ip>:8787/health` from the phone browser. If it does not return\n`{\"ok\":true}`, confirm the phone and computer are on the same Wi-Fi network,\nclient isolation is disabled, and your firewall allows Node.js on the Hono port\nand Metro port `8081`.\n\n### Android emulator cannot reach `127.0.0.1`\n\nUse `http://10.0.2.2:8787` for\n`EXPO_PUBLIC_TANSTACK_AI_BASE_URL`. Android emulators map `10.0.2.2` to the\nhost machine.\n\n### Expo prints Android SDK or `adb` warnings\n\nThis is an Android tooling issue, not a TanStack AI transport issue. Confirm\nAndroid Studio installed the SDK, an emulator exists in Device Manager, and\n`adb` is on `PATH`. On Windows, check\n`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Android\\Sdk\\platform-tools\\adb.exe`.\n\n### The phone logs `UnsupportedResponseStreamError`\n\nYour runtime does not expose streaming `fetch`, `Response.body.getReader()`, or\n`TextDecoder`. Switch from `fetchHttpStream()` to `xhrHttpStream()` or\n`xhrServerSentEvents()`. Do not rely on fetch polyfills unless they provide a\nreal incremental readable stream.\n\n### XHR reports a server error\n\nCheck the Hono server terminal first. Common causes are missing\n`OPENAI_API_KEY`, an unsupported `OPENAI_MODEL`, or pointing\n`xhrServerSentEvents()` at `/chat/http` instead of `/chat/sse` (or the reverse).\n\nYou now have the full React Native path: a server-owned provider boundary, a\nnative-reachable URL, a mobile-compatible transport, and an Expo example that\nproves the setup on a real device.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: \"Quick Start: React Native\"\nid: quick-start-react-native\norder: 3\ndescription: \"Build a React Native or Expo chat screen with TanStack AI's useChat hook, a server-only OpenAI backend, and mobile-compatible streaming transports.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - react native\n  - expo\n  - mobile\n  - useChat\n  - streaming\n  - xhrHttpStream\n  - openai\n---\n\nYou have a React Native or Expo app and you want to add streaming AI chat\nwithout putting provider SDKs or API keys in the native bundle. By the end of\nthis guide, your app will call a server-owned Hono route with `useChat` from\n`@tanstack/ai-react`, stream responses over a mobile-compatible transport, and\nkeep `OPENAI_API_KEY` / `OPENAI_MODEL` on the server.\n\n> **Coming from the web quick start?** The hook is the same, but the URL and\n> transport are different. React Native needs an absolute backend URL, not\n> `/api/chat`, and most Expo runtimes should start with `xhrHttpStream()`.\n\n## 1. Install packages\n\nIf you are starting from scratch, create an Expo app first:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"local-install\" -->\n\nreact: create-expo-app@latest my-ai-chat\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nInstall TanStack AI, the React hook package, the OpenAI adapter for your\nserver, and Hono for the example backend:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"install\" -->\n\nreact: @tanstack/ai @tanstack/ai-react @tanstack/ai-openai hono @hono/node-server zod\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\nIf your Expo app lives in a workspace, run the command from the app package or\nuse your workspace filter.\n\n## 2. Keep OpenAI on the server\n\nCreate a Hono route that owns the model, API key, and response format. The\nnative app sends chat messages to this route; it never imports\n`@tanstack/ai-openai` and never receives `OPENAI_API_KEY`.\n\n```ts\n// server.ts\nimport { serve } from '@hono/node-server'\nimport { chat, toHttpResponse, toServerSentEventsResponse } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { openaiText } from '@tanstack/ai-openai'\nimport { Hono } from 'hono'\nimport { model } from './config'\n\nconst app = new Hono()\n\nfunction requireOpenAIKey() {\n  if (!process.env.OPENAI_API_KEY) {\n    throw new Error('OPENAI_API_KEY is not configured on the server')\n  }\n}\n\napp.get('/health', (c) => c.json({ ok: true }))\n\napp.post('/chat/http', async (c) => {\n  requireOpenAIKey()\n  const body = await c.req.json()\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(model),\n    messages: body.messages,\n  })\n\n  return toHttpResponse(stream, {\n    headers: {\n      'Content-Type': 'application/x-ndjson',\n      'Cache-Control': 'no-cache',\n    },\n  })\n})\n\napp.post('/chat/sse', async (c) => {\n  requireOpenAIKey()\n  const body = await c.req.json()\n  const stream = chat({\n    adapter: openaiText(model),\n    messages: body.messages,\n  })\n\n  return toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)\n})\n\nserve({\n  fetch: app.fetch,\n  hostname: '0.0.0.0',\n  port: Number(process.env.PORT ?? 8787),\n})\n```\n\nSet server-only environment variables where the Hono process runs:\n\n```env\nOPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...\nOPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.2\n```\n\nRun the Hono server before starting the native app. For a TypeScript-only\nexample, install `tsx` and add a script:\n\n<!-- ::start:tabs variant=\"package-manager\" mode=\"dev-install\" -->\n\nreact: tsx\n\n<!-- ::end:tabs -->\n\n```bash\npnpm pkg set scripts.dev:server=\"tsx server.ts\"\npnpm dev:server\n```\n\n> **Route pairing matters:** `xhrHttpStream()` and `fetchHttpStream()` expect\n> the newline-delimited JSON response from `toHttpResponse()`.\n> `xhrServerSentEvents()` expects the `text/event-stream` response from\n> `toServerSentEventsResponse()`.\n\n## 3. Configure a native-reachable URL\n\nReact Native is not served from your backend origin, so `/api/chat` cannot work\nas a default. Expose the backend URL to Expo with a public variable:\n\n```env\nEXPO_PUBLIC_TANSTACK_AI_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.10:8787\n```\n\nUse the address your device can reach:\n\n- iOS simulator: `http://127.0.0.1:8787` often works.\n- Android emulator: use `http://10.0.2.2:8787`.\n- Physical device: use your computer's LAN IP, for example\n  `http://192.168.1.10:8787`, or a tunneled HTTPS URL.\n\nOnly `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` values are bundled into the app. Keep provider keys as\nplain server variables such as `OPENAI_API_KEY`.\n\n## 4. Use `useChat` in your native screen\n\nStart with `xhrHttpStream()` for Expo and React Native. It reads the same\nnewline-delimited JSON produced by `toHttpResponse()` and relies on XHR progress\nevents, which are usually more reliable on phone runtimes than streaming\n`fetch`.\n\n```tsx\n// ChatScreen.tsx\nimport { useState } from 'react'\nimport { Button, ScrollView, Text, TextInput, View } from 'react-native'\nimport { useChat, xhrHttpStream } from '@tanstack/ai-react'\n\nconst baseUrl =\n  process.env.EXPO_PUBLIC_TANSTACK_AI_BASE_URL ?? 'http://127.0.0.1:8787'\n\nexport function ChatScreen() {\n  const [input, setInput] = useState('')\n  const { messages, sendMessage, isLoading, error } = useChat({\n    connection: xhrHttpStream(`${baseUrl}/chat/http`),\n  })\n\n  async function send() {\n    const text = input.trim()\n    if (!text || isLoading) return\n    setInput('')\n    await sendMessage(text)\n  }\n\n  return (\n    <View style={{ flex: 1, padding: 24, gap: 12 }}>\n      <ScrollView style={{ flex: 1 }}>\n        {messages.map((message) => (\n          <View key={message.id} style={{ marginBottom: 16 }}>\n            <Text style={{ fontWeight: '700' }}>{message.role}</Text>\n            {message.parts.map((part, index) =>\n              part.type === 'text' ? (\n                <Text key={index}>{part.content}</Text>\n              ) : null,\n            )}\n          </View>\n        ))}\n      </ScrollView>\n\n      {error ? <Text style={{ color: 'crimson' }}>{error.message}</Text> : null}\n\n      <TextInput\n        value={input}\n        onChangeText={setInput}\n        editable={!isLoading}\n        placeholder=\"Ask for a recipe...\"\n        style={{ borderWidth: 1, borderRadius: 8, padding: 12 }}\n      />\n      <Button title={isLoading ? 'Streaming...' : 'Send'} onPress={send} />\n    </View>\n  )\n}\n```\n\nYou now have a native chat screen that calls your server endpoint, streams\nassistant text, and keeps provider credentials outside the app.\n\n## 5. Choose a transport deliberately\n\nUse the transport that matches your server route and runtime:\n\n| Native runtime | Client adapter | Server response |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| Most Expo / React Native apps | `xhrHttpStream(url)` with `/chat/http` | `toHttpResponse(stream)` |\n| SSE-compatible native runtime or proxy path | `xhrServerSentEvents(url)` with `/chat/sse` | `toServerSentEventsResponse(stream)` |\n| Runtime with streaming `fetch` support | `fetchHttpStream(url)` with `/chat/http` | `toHttpResponse(stream)` |\n\nOnly use `fetchHttpStream()` when your exact runtime supports all of:\n\n- `Response.body`\n- `Response.body.getReader()`\n- `TextDecoder`\n\nIf any of those are missing, the adapter throws\n`UnsupportedResponseStreamError`. A polyfilled `fetch` that buffers the whole\nresponse is not enough; TanStack AI needs incremental response bytes to update\nthe chat while the model is streaming.\n\nFor deeper adapter options such as headers, credentials, `withCredentials`, and\ndynamic URLs, see [Request Options](../transports/request-options).\n\n## 6. Try the Expo recipe example\n\nIf you are evaluating React Native support, use the included Expo app. It runs a\nlocal Hono/OpenAI server, shows a transport selector, and streams structured\nrecipe cards so you can verify native chat and structured output behavior\ntogether.\n\nCreate `examples/ts-react-native-chat/.env`:\n\n```env\nOPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...\nOPENAI_MODEL=gpt-5.2\n```\n\nRun the example:\n\n```bash\npnpm --filter ts-react-native-chat dev\n```\n\nThe command starts:\n\n- Hono on `0.0.0.0:8787`\n- Expo/Metro in LAN mode\n- `EXPO_PUBLIC_TANSTACK_AI_BASE_URL=http://<lan-ip>:8787` when a LAN address is detected\n\nScan the Expo Go QR code from a phone on the same Wi-Fi network. In the app,\nuse the Testing mode panel to switch between Fetch HTTP, XHR HTTP, and XHR SSE.\nThe main recipe card streams structured fields such as title, ingredients,\nsteps, tips, warnings, and revision across follow-up prompts.\n\nFor example-specific commands and network overrides, see\n`examples/ts-react-native-chat/README.md`.\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### `http://localhost:8081` shows JSON\n\nThat is normal. Port `8081` is Metro's manifest and bundle server, not a web UI.\nLaunch the app from Expo Go, an Android emulator, or an iOS simulator instead.\n\n### A physical device cannot reach the backend\n\nOpen `http://<lan-ip>:8787/health` from the phone browser. If it does not return\n`{\"ok\":true}`, confirm the phone and computer are on the same Wi-Fi network,\nclient isolation is disabled, and your firewall allows Node.js on the Hono port\nand Metro port `8081`.\n\n### Android emulator cannot reach `127.0.0.1`\n\nUse `http://10.0.2.2:8787` for\n`EXPO_PUBLIC_TANSTACK_AI_BASE_URL`. Android emulators map `10.0.2.2` to the\nhost machine.\n\n### Expo prints Android SDK or `adb` warnings\n\nThis is an Android tooling issue, not a TanStack AI transport issue. Confirm\nAndroid Studio installed the SDK, an emulator exists in Device Manager, and\n`adb` is on `PATH`. On Windows, check\n`%LOCALAPPDATA%\\Android\\Sdk\\platform-tools\\adb.exe`.\n\n### The phone logs `UnsupportedResponseStreamError`\n\nYour runtime does not expose streaming `fetch`, `Response.body.getReader()`, or\n`TextDecoder`. Switch from `fetchHttpStream()` to `xhrHttpStream()` or\n`xhrServerSentEvents()`. Do not rely on fetch polyfills unless they provide a\nreal incremental readable stream.\n\n### XHR reports a server error\n\nCheck the Hono server terminal first. Common causes are missing\n`OPENAI_API_KEY`, an unsupported `OPENAI_MODEL`, or pointing\n`xhrServerSentEvents()` at `/chat/http` instead of `/chat/sse` (or the reverse).\n\nYou now have the full React Native path: a server-owned provider boundary, a\nnative-reachable URL, a mobile-compatible transport, and an Expo example that\nproves the setup on a real device.\n"}
